 "corporate_story": [
  "MIR paid 17 times by 31 August, $151,872 including HST ($134,400 before HST); the full year projects to $208,320. Cash stood at $163,061.21 on 31 August after $55,000 moved to Wealthsimple.",
  "The T2 2025 was filed and assessed on 18 May and its $4,592 refund arrived on 28 May as $4,644.90. That deposit is not revenue and must come out of the 2026 workbook totals.",
  "Instalments are paid at about $900 a month ($6,900 by August) instead of CRA's $13,370 schedule. The 7 October projection puts 2026 tax about $4,743 above planned instalments. Lease payments over the s.67.3 cap ($11,564.77) explain about $1,411 of that and the non deductible 20% personal share of the Mercedes $578; the rest is profit. Topping up would take about $1,186 a month from September to December.",
  "Maham's pay runs from April at $2,666.67 a month with $460.14 sent to CRA each month. The Mercedes stays at 80% business use; the 20% personal share ($7,119.48 for 2026) is charged to Umar against what the corporation owes him, which was $16,111.98 on 23 September.",
  "The HST year ending 14 August 2026 shows a $2,404.66 refund after the Mercedes claim was cut to 80% on 7 October. Saira, back as accountant since September, files it by 16 November and will prepare the T2 2026."
 ],
 "personal_story": [
  "No 2026 personal documents are on file yet. Maham earns $24,000 from the corporation for April to December; both personal returns are due 30 April 2027."
